# Linkedin Ads MCP server for AI agents and assistants
Securely connect your AI agents and chatbots (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, etc) with Linkedin Ads MCP or direct API to manage campaigns, review ad performance, analyze spend, and publish organization social content through natural language.

Linkedin Ads is LinkedIn's marketing platform for creating, managing, and measuring paid campaigns across LinkedIn. It helps teams reach professional audiences with precise targeting, campaign analytics, and sponsored content tools.

## Connect Linkedin Ads MCP Tool with your Agent
1
#### Install Composio
typescript
```
npm install @composio/core ai @ai-sdk/mcp @ai-sdk/openai
```
Install the Composio SDK and your agent framework
2
#### Create a session with MCP enabled
typescript
```
import { Composio } from "@composio/core";
const composio = new Composio();
const { mcp } = await composio.create("your-user-id", {
toolkits: ["linkedin_ads"],
mcp: true,
});
```
Create a session scoped to Linkedin Ads and read its MCP URL and headers
3
#### Connect your agent to the MCP server
typescript
```
import { createMCPClient } from "@ai-sdk/mcp";
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai";
import { generateText, stepCountIs } from "ai";
const client = await createMCPClient({
transport: { type: "http", url: mcp.url, headers: mcp.headers },
});
const { text } = await generateText({
model: openai("gpt-5.6-sol"),
tools: await client.tools(),
prompt: "List active LinkedIn ad campaigns with spend and impressions",
stopWhen: stepCountIs(10),
});
console.log(text);
await client.close();
```
Pass the session's MCP URL and headers to your agent and run a Linkedin Ads request

### AI Native Linkedin Ads Integration
- Supports both Linkedin Ads MCP and direct API based integrations
- Structured, LLM-friendly schemas for reliable campaign, creative, and analytics actions
- Rich coverage for reading, writing, and querying your Linkedin Ads marketing data
### Managed Auth
- Built-in OAuth handling with automatic token refresh and rotation once your LinkedIn app is configured
- Central place to manage, scope, and revoke Linkedin Ads access
- Per user and per environment credentials instead of hard-coded keys

Managed auth, hosted MCP servers, and every Linkedin Ads tool your agent needs.Free to start.
